# Sasscout backend reverse proxy (STEP 31) — Caddy.
#
# Production architecture:
#
#     Public Internet
#            ↓  HTTPS/TLS (terminated HERE)
#         Caddy
#            ↓  HTTP to backend on a private network
#     Sasscout Backend  (does NOT terminate TLS itself)
#
# Caddy terminates TLS and forwards plain HTTP to the backend, setting
# X-Forwarded-For (real client IP) and X-Forwarded-Proto for the backend's
# trusted-proxy handling (TRUST_PROXY=true on the backend).
#
# This Caddyfile is the LOCAL HTTPS test variant: it serves HTTPS on :8080 and
# proxies to the `backend` compose service. `tls internal` uses Caddy's internal
# CA (self-signed for localhost) — remove it and use your real domain in
# production to get automatic Let's Encrypt HTTPS.

:8080 {
	tls internal

	reverse_proxy backend:3001
}
